{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 13:18:39", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-eb9c0224-4145-4c46-8081-5ca5801da49b', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Local Claude Integration"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_015bjxd29siA2qNCRYUpkaFZ', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CNBJrw92wjpLs3WmSVD7M2', 'name': 'git_status', 'input': {'include_history': True, 'history_count': 5}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_015bjxd29siA2qNCRYUpkaFZ', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Local Claude Integration - Requirements Document\\n\\n## Project Overview\\n\\n### Vision\\nAdd support for a local Claude CLI instance as an alternative AI provider that takes priority over the Anthropic API when available, functional, and reliable. This creates a hybrid approach where the system automatically prefers local execution but gracefully falls back to the API when needed.\\n\\n### Problem Statement\\nCurrently, the ensemble system exclusively uses the Anthropic API for all AI operations through `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` and `model_router.py`. This means:\\n- All requests incur API costs\\n- System depends entirely on external API availability\\n- No ability to leverage local compute resources\\n- No way to use the user\'s local Claude CLI subscription\\n\\n### Solution\\nCreate a new **Local Claude Provider** that:\\n1. Executes prompts via the local Claude CLI (`/opt/homebrew/bin/claude`)\\n2. Integrates with the existing `model_router.py` provider system\\n3. Implements health checking and reliability tracking\\n4. Falls back to API automatically when local execution fails\\n\\n## Objectives\\n\\n### Primary Objectives\\n1. **Local First**: System prefers local Claude CLI when available and healthy\\n2. **Seamless Fallback**: Automatic fallback to Anthropic API on local failure\\n3. **Health Tracking**: Monitor local provider reliability for intelligent routing\\n4. **Zero Breaking Changes**: Existing API-based flow continues working unchanged\\n\\n### Secondary Objectives\\n1. **Cost Visibility**: Track which provider handled each request\\n2. **Performance Metrics**: Compare local vs API response times\\n3. **Configuration**: Allow enabling/disabling local provider via settings\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\n### In Scope\\n1. Create `LocalClaudeProvider` class that executes prompts via CLI\\n2. Add local provider to `model_router.py` provider registry\\n3. Implement health check for local Claude availability\\n4. Add provider preference logic (local \\u2192 API fallback)\\n5. Track provider usage in metrics/activity system\\n6. Handle CLI-specific response format conversion\\n7. Support system prompts via `--system-prompt` flag\\n8. Support model selection via `--model` flag\\n\\n### Out of Scope\\n- MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration\\n- Tool execution through local Claude (tools stay API-only for now)\\n- Session/conversation continuity across providers\\n- Multi-provider load balancing (we use preference order, not round-robin)\\n- Real-time streaming (use `--print` mode for simplicity)\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n\\n### Local Claude CLI Specifications\\n- **Location**: `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` (v2.1.12)\\n- **Non-interactive Mode**: `--print` or `-p` flag required\\n- **JSON Output**: `--output-format json` for structured responses\\n- **System Prompt**: `--system-prompt <prompt>` flag\\n- **Model Selection**: `--model <model>` (e.g., `sonnet`, `opus`, or full model ID)\\n- **Response Format**: JSON with `type`, `result`, `usage`, `total_cost_usd`, etc.\\n\\n### Existing System Integration Points\\n1. **`src/runtime/agents/model_router.py`**\\n   - Has `Provider` enum including `LOCAL` \\n   - Has `QualityTier` including `LOCAL`\\n   - Model catalog structure supports local models\\n   - `_check_local_model()` method exists but returns False\\n\\n2. **`src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`**\\n   - `AgentRuntime` class handles all execution\\n   - Uses `Anthropic` client directly for API calls\\n   - Token tracking, metrics, activity logging already in place\\n\\n3. **`src/runtime/agents/model_selector.py`**\\n   - Static tier-based model selection\\n   - Could be extended for local preference\\n\\n## Requirements\\n\\n### Functional Requirements\\n\\n#### FR-1: Local Provider Implementation\\n- **FR-1.1**: Create `LocalClaudeProvider` class that wraps CLI execution\\n- **FR-1.2**: Provider must accept: prompt text, system prompt, model selection\\n- **FR-1.3**: Provider must return: result text, token usage, cost, duration\\n- **FR-1.4**: Provider must handle CLI errors gracefully\\n\\n#### FR-2: Health Checking\\n- **FR-2.1**: Check if `claude` CLI is installed and executable\\n- **FR-2.2**: Perform lightweight health check before routing to local\\n- **FR-2.3**: Track consecutive failures to avoid repeated local attempts\\n- **FR-2.4**: Auto-recover: retry local after cooldown period (e.g., 60s)\\n\\n#### FR-3: Provider Selection\\n- **FR-3.1**: When local healthy \\u2192 route to local provider\\n- **FR-3.2**: When local unhealthy/unavailable \\u2192 route to Anthropic API\\n- **FR-3.3**: Record which provider was used for each request\\n- **FR-3.4**: Allow configuration to disable local provider entirely\\n\\n#### FR-4: Response Handling\\n- **FR-4.1**: Parse JSON output from CLI (`--output-format json`)\\n- **FR-4.2**: Extract `result` field as response text\\n- **FR-4.3**: Extract `usage` for token tracking\\n- **FR-4.4**: Extract `total_cost_usd` for cost tracking\\n\\n### Non-Functional Requirements\\n\\n#### NFR-1: Performance\\n- Local provider overhead should be < 100ms beyond CLI execution time\\n- Fallback should occur within 5 seconds of local failure\\n\\n#### NFR-2: Reliability\\n- System must never fail completely if local provider fails\\n- API fallback must always be available as safety net\\n\\n#### NFR-3: Observability\\n- Log provider selection decisions\\n- Track success/failure rates by provider\\n- Include provider info in activity tracker records\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n\\n1. \\u2705 Local Claude CLI can be used for agent execution when available\\n2. \\u2705 System automatically falls back to API when local unavailable\\n3. \\u2705 Provider selection is logged and visible in activity/metrics\\n4. \\u2705 No breaking changes to existing API-based workflows\\n5. \\u2705 Tests cover local provider, health checking, and fallback logic\\n\\n## Architecture Decisions\\n\\n### Decision 1: CLI-based Integration\\n**Choice**: Use subprocess to call `claude` CLI rather than importing SDK\\n**Rationale**: \\n- CLI is already installed and authenticated\\n- Simpler integration with existing auth/subscription\\n- Avoids SDK version conflicts\\n\\n### Decision 2: Synchronous Execution\\n**Choice**: Use `--print` mode for synchronous responses\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Simpler integration with existing sync runtime\\n- Streaming can be added later if needed\\n- JSON output is easier to parse\\n\\n### Decision 3: Health Check Circuit Breaker\\n**Choice**: Track failures and implement cooldown before retrying local\\n**Rationale**:\\n- Prevents repeated slow failures\\n- Allows automatic recovery\\n- Matches existing `CircuitBreaker` pattern in codebase\\n\\n## File Changes Required\\n\\n### New Files\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/local_claude_provider.py` - Local provider implementation\\n\\n### Modified Files\\n1. `src/runtime/agents/model_router.py` - Add local provider integration\\n2. `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py` - Use provider selection for execution\\n3. `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py` - Track provider used\\n\\n### Test Files\\n1. `tests/test_local_claude_provider.py` - Unit tests for local provider\\n2. `tests/test_model_router_local.py` - Integration tests for routing\\n\\n## Assumptions Made\\n1. User has Claude CLI installed at `/opt/homebrew/bin/claude` (can be made configurable)\\n2. Claude CLI is already authenticated with user\'s subscription\\n3. Local execution provides equivalent model access to API\\n4. JSON output format is stable across CLI versions\\n5. System prompt and model flags work as documented\\n\\n## Open Questions (To Be Resolved During Implementation)\\n1. Should we support tool execution through local CLI? (Initially: No)\\n2. Should we support streaming for local provider? (Initially: No)\\n3. How should we handle very long prompts that may exceed CLI argument limits? (Use temp file)\\n4. Should health check be cached per-process or persisted? (Per-process for simplicity)\\n"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CNBJrw92wjpLs3WmSVD7M2', 'content': '{"success": true, "current_branch": "main", "changes": {"staged": [{"file": "ogs/ensemble-backend.log.1", "status": "M"}], "unstaged": [{"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.2", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.3", "status": "M"}, {"file": "logs/ensemble-backend.log.4", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md", "status": "M"}, {"file": "src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks.md", "status": "M"}], "untracked": ["src/field/ensemble_ui/output/model_update_report.md"]}, "has_changes": true, "clean": false, "ahead": 0, "behind": 0, "last_commit": {"hash": "ff6f888c307d2894bd9b20857ede490b350dcf10", "message": "Fix self-improvement system to make real changes instead of useless text injection", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "11 minutes ago"}, "history": [{"hash": "ff6f888c307d2894bd9b20857ede490b350dcf10", "message": "Fix self-improvement system to make real changes instead of useless text injection", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "11 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "0d4a7d3cc5531c85bbd7e7a80d823aeea6f830a2", "message": "Complete model optimization for Frontend Coordinator: update from haiku to sonnet for cost efficiency", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "16 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "40dd4ec08ea8a76ef630d03c128aaecc2231fff5", "message": "Update Frontend Coordinator model preference from \'haiku\' to \'sonnet\'", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "17 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "1f1586e1a8902c3e35073ac3d73904dbbf414a7f", "message": "Update Test Coordinator model preference to sonnet for cost optimization", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "17 minutes ago"}, {"hash": "93bb03839a0303fc577a7d2491f99b39c4436510", "message": "Update Frontend Coordinator model preference from \'haiku\' to \'sonnet\' for cost optimization", "author": "Matt Billock", "when": "17 minutes ago"}], "stash_count": 0}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01H8euRGGnrVn55Q1Bu91S9u', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Local Claude Integration', 'description': 'Add support for a local Claude CLI instance as an alternative AI provider that takes priority over the Anthropic API when available, functional, and reliable. This creates a hybrid approach where the system automatically prefers local execution but gracefully falls back to the API when needed.'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01H8euRGGnrVn55Q1Bu91S9u', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "ad1fd4d8", "message": "Created project: Local Claude Integration", "summary": {"project_id": "ad1fd4d8", "project_name": "Local Claude Integration", "description": "Add support for a local Claude CLI instance as an alternative AI provider that takes priority over the Anthropic API when available, functional, and reliable. This creates a hybrid approach where the system automatically prefers local execution but gracefully falls back to the API when needed.", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-17T13:15:52.520044", "updated_at": "2026-01-17T13:15:52.520044", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-17T13:15:52.520044", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Local Claude Integration\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Kw9JEjfkDbuBGYZANx4Ayw', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Local Claude Integration - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nAdd support for a local Claude CLI instance as an alternative AI provider that takes priority over the Anthropic API when available, functional, and reliable.\n\n## Milestones\n\n### Milestone 1: Local Provider Core Implementation\n**Objective**: Create the LocalClaudeProvider class with CLI execution and health checking capabilities.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. `src/runtime/agents/local_claude_provider.py` - Core provider implementation\n   - CLI wrapper for subprocess execution\n   - JSON response parsing\n   - Error handling and timeout management\n   - Health check with circuit breaker pattern\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- LocalClaudeProvider can execute prompts via CLI\n- Properly parses JSON output (result, usage, cost)\n- Health check detects if CLI is installed/executable\n- Circuit breaker tracks failures and implements cooldown\n- Handles CLI errors gracefully without crashing\n\n**Dependencies**: None\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 2: Model Router Integration\n**Objective**: Integrate local provider into the model_router.py provider selection system.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. Modified `src/runtime/agents/model_router.py`\n   - Register local provider\n   - Implement provider preference logic (local → API fallback)\n   - Make `_check_local_model()` functional\n   - Add configuration option to enable/disable local provider\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Model router prefers local provider when healthy\n- Falls back to API when local unavailable/unhealthy\n- Configuration flag to disable local provider works\n- Provider selection is logged\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (LocalClaudeProvider must exist)\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 3: Runtime Integration & Activity Tracking\n**Objective**: Update runtime.py to use provider selection and track provider usage in activity system.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. Modified `src/runtime/agents/runtime.py`\n   - Use model router for provider selection\n   - Execute via local provider when selected\n   - Handle provider-specific execution paths\n\n2. Modified `src/runtime/agents/activity_tracker.py`\n   - Track which provider handled each request\n   - Log provider selection decisions\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- AgentRuntime routes to local provider when selected\n- API fallback works seamlessly on local failure\n- Activity tracker records provider info\n- No breaking changes to existing workflows\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2\n\n---\n\n### Milestone 4: Testing & Verification\n**Objective**: Comprehensive test coverage for local provider, routing, and fallback logic.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n1. `tests/test_local_claude_provider.py` - Unit tests\n   - CLI execution mocking\n   - Response parsing tests\n   - Health check tests\n   - Circuit breaker tests\n\n2. `tests/test_model_router_local.py` - Integration tests\n   - Provider selection logic\n   - Fallback scenarios\n   - Configuration tests\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Unit tests pass for local provider\n- Integration tests verify routing logic\n- Fallback tests demonstrate API recovery\n- All existing tests still pass\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestones 1, 2, 3\n\n---\n\n## Timeline Summary\n\n| Milestone | Description | Dependencies | Estimated Complexity |\n|-----------|-------------|--------------|---------------------|\n| M1 | Local Provider Core | None | Medium |\n| M2 | Model Router Integration | M1 | Medium |\n| M3 | Runtime & Activity Tracking | M1, M2 | Medium |\n| M4 | Testing & Verification | M1, M2, M3 | Medium |\n\n## Risk Mitigation\n\n1. **CLI Unavailability**: Design assumes CLI may not be present; fallback is core feature\n2. **Long Prompts**: Use temp file for prompts exceeding CLI argument limits\n3. **Response Format Changes**: Parse defensively, log warnings on unexpected formats\n4. **Performance**: Keep overhead under 100ms; use synchronous execution for simplicity\n\n## Success Metrics\n\n- ✅ Local Claude CLI can be used for agent execution when available\n- ✅ System automatically falls back to API when local unavailable\n- ✅ Provider selection is logged and visible in activity/metrics\n- ✅ No breaking changes to existing API-based workflows\n- ✅ Tests cover local provider, health checking, and fallback logic\n'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01TSABJXdmZkLskXMkUuz7rB', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'ad1fd4d8', 'description': 'Milestone 1: Create LocalClaudeProvider class with CLI execution, JSON parsing, health checking, and circuit breaker pattern', 'assigned_to': 'tdd_coordinator'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01NobCzfKre8DwKjn1jQY3TN', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'ad1fd4d8', 'description': 'Milestone 2: Integrate local provider into model_router.py with preference logic and configuration', 'assigned_to': 'tdd_coordinator'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01KiGrWnZr8pwLokHhxhcujR', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'ad1fd4d8', 'description': 'Milestone 3: Update runtime.py for provider selection and activity_tracker.py for provider tracking', 'assigned_to': 'tdd_coordinator'}}, {'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01Uat5owzyvB2arMuSN9YMcK', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_task', 'project_id': 'ad1fd4d8', 'description': 'Milestone 4: Comprehensive testing - unit tests for local provider and integration tests for routing', 'assigned_to': 'tdd_coordinator'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Kw9JEjfkDbuBGYZANx4Ayw', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260117_131614.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260117_131614.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01TSABJXdmZkLskXMkUuz7rB', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "4437994a", "message": "Added task: Milestone 1: Create LocalClaudeProvider class with CLI execution, JSON parsing, health checking, and circuit breaker pattern"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01NobCzfKre8DwKjn1jQY3TN', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "5d57dfa9", "message": "Added task: Milestone 2: Integrate local provider into model_router.py with preference logic and configuration"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01KiGrWnZr8pwLokHhxhcujR', 'content': '{"success": true, "task_id": "2e2af4af", "message": "Added task: Milestone 3: Update runtime.py for provider selection and activity_tracker.py for provider tracking"}'}, {'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01Ua