{"timestamp": "2026-01-17 15:19:05", "level": "DEBUG", "module": "anthropic._base_client", "message": "Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-dd966338-7a22-4f8f-bf5e-ee90463b53d6', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4096, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Please complete the following task:\n\n{\n  "requirements_file": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md",\n  "output_directory": "/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output",\n  "project_name": "Timeline Page Data Refresh Architecture",\n  "project_id": "01a20f68"\n}\n\nRemember to respond with valid JSON matching the expected output format.\n'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01CXh4eFAKTV381s3nWXjc96', 'name': 'read_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/requirements.md'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01CXh4eFAKTV381s3nWXjc96', 'content': '{"success": true, "content": "# Timeline Page Data Refresh Architecture Requirements\\n\\n## Problem Statement\\nPrevent view disruption during data refresh while maintaining real-time updates for the Timeline Page.\\n\\n## Objectives\\n1. Identify current data refresh mechanism causing view disruption\\n2. Design an architecture that supports seamless data updates\\n3. Minimize performance impact during refresh operations\\n4. Maintain real-time data consistency\\n\\n## Technical Constraints\\n- Must not block UI during data refresh\\n- Preserve user interaction during updates\\n- Support incremental and full data refreshes\\n- Minimize memory and computational overhead\\n\\n## Success Criteria\\n- No visual interruption during data refresh\\n- Less than 50ms latency for update propagation\\n- Ability to handle large datasets efficiently\\n- Graceful error handling for network or data source issues\\n\\n## Proposed Investigation Areas\\n1. Current data fetching and rendering mechanism\\n2. State management approach\\n3. Potential caching strategies\\n4. Incremental update techniques\\n5. Optimistic UI update patterns\\n\\n## Out of Scope\\n- Complete UI redesign\\n- Changes to backend data source\\n- Modifications to authentication system"}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VbuF7vveHLRBWof1SgCmHf', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'create_project', 'project_name': 'Timeline Page Data Refresh Architecture', 'description': 'Design and implement architecture to prevent view disruption during data refresh while maintaining real-time updates for the Timeline Page'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VbuF7vveHLRBWof1SgCmHf', 'content': '{"success": true, "project_id": "3b9b5041", "message": "Created project: Timeline Page Data Refresh Architecture", "summary": {"project_id": "3b9b5041", "project_name": "Timeline Page Data Refresh Architecture", "description": "Design and implement architecture to prevent view disruption during data refresh while maintaining real-time updates for the Timeline Page", "status": "active", "created_at": "2026-01-17T15:18:51.158860", "updated_at": "2026-01-17T15:18:51.158860", "task_counts": {"total": 0, "todo": 0, "in_progress": 0, "completed": 0, "blocked": 0, "cancelled": 0}, "completion_percentage": 0.0, "recent_notes": [{"timestamp": "2026-01-17T15:18:51.158860", "author": "executive_director", "note": "Project \'Timeline Page Data Refresh Architecture\' created", "category": "milestone"}], "output_directory": null}}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01MRx2sLfbSWHjQf7TLxvjWY', 'name': 'write_file', 'input': {'file_path': '/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md', 'content': '# Timeline Page Data Refresh Architecture - Milestone Plan\n\n## Project Overview\nPrevent view disruption during data refresh while maintaining real-time updates for the Timeline Page.\n\n## Milestone 1: Analysis & Architecture Design (Foundation)\n**Objective**: Analyze current system and design optimal refresh architecture\n**Duration**: 3-5 days\n**Deliverables**:\n- Current system analysis report\n- Comprehensive architecture design\n- Data flow diagrams\n- Performance requirements specification\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Complete analysis of current data refresh mechanism\n- Architecture design supporting <50ms update latency\n- Clear separation between incremental and full refresh strategies\n- Documented error handling approach\n\n**Dependencies**: None (foundation milestone)\n\n## Milestone 2: Core Infrastructure Implementation\n**Objective**: Implement foundational architecture components\n**Duration**: 5-7 days\n**Deliverables**:\n- State management system with optimistic updates\n- Caching layer implementation\n- Data fetching abstraction with non-blocking operations\n- Basic incremental update mechanism\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Non-blocking data refresh operations\n- State management preserves UI interactions\n- Caching reduces redundant network requests\n- Unit tests for core components\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 1 (requires architecture design)\n\n## Milestone 3: Timeline Integration & Testing\n**Objective**: Integrate refresh architecture with Timeline Page\n**Duration**: 4-6 days\n**Deliverables**:\n- Timeline Page integration\n- Comprehensive test suite\n- Performance optimization\n- Error handling implementation\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- No visual interruption during data refresh\n- Performance meets <50ms latency requirement\n- Graceful handling of network/data source issues\n- Integration tests covering all refresh scenarios\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 2 (requires core infrastructure)\n\n## Milestone 4: Optimization & Documentation\n**Objective**: Final optimization and project documentation\n**Duration**: 2-3 days\n**Deliverables**:\n- Performance optimization\n- User documentation\n- Technical documentation\n- Deployment guide\n\n**Acceptance Criteria**:\n- Efficient handling of large datasets\n- Complete documentation set\n- Ready for production deployment\n- Performance benchmarks documented\n\n**Dependencies**: Milestone 3 (requires complete implementation)\n\n## Total Project Duration: 14-21 days\n## Critical Success Factors:\n- Maintain current functionality while enhancing performance\n- Ensure seamless user experience\n- Implement robust error handling\n- Meet strict performance requirements'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01MRx2sLfbSWHjQf7TLxvjWY', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "File written successfully to /Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md (backup: /Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260117_151902.md)", "backup_path": "/Users/mattbillock/.ensemble/backups/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan_20260117_151902.md", "was_overwrite": true}'}]}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_use', 'id': 'toolu_01VQgT68CJhxhvsJCGXGcRr6', 'name': 'project_tracking', 'input': {'action': 'add_note', 'project_id': '3b9b5041', 'note': 'Created comprehensive milestone plan with 4 milestones covering analysis, infrastructure, integration, and optimization phases', 'category': 'milestone'}}]}, {'role': 'user', 'content': [{'type': 'tool_result', 'tool_use_id': 'toolu_01VQgT68CJhxhvsJCGXGcRr6', 'content': '{"success": true, "message": "Added note to project"}'}]}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a Development Manager agent.\n\n## Purpose\nDrives implementation from requirements through delivery. Breaks projects into milestones, identifies requirements gaps, drives architecture via System Architect and task breakdown via Coordinators, then coordinates with TDD Coordinator for implementation. Reports to Executive Director.\n\n## Instructions\nYou drive the show from concept through performance. Report to Executive Director, coordinate System Architect/Coordinators/TDD Coordinator.\n\n**CRITICAL RULES:**\n1. **NEVER write code yourself** - you lack can_write_code permission\n2. **If spawn_agent fails, STOP and return error** - DO NOT write code as fallback\n3. **Execute ALL steps sequentially** - don\'t stop after planning\n4. **Use EXACT agent paths** - see examples below\n5. **SPAWN VALIDATION REQUIRED** - See [Common Instructions - Spawn Agent Validation](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/common_instructions.md#spawn-agent-validation) - ALL spawn_agent calls MUST use ACTUAL VALUES, not placeholders\n\n### Directory Structure\n\n**CRITICAL - READ FIRST**: See [Directory Structure Guide](/Users/mattbillock/Development/ai_exploration/ensemble/docs/DIRECTORY_STRUCTURE.md) for complete file organization rules.\n\n**Your Write Locations** (Documentation Only):\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/architecture.md` - Architecture documents\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/milestone_plan.md` - Milestone plans\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/backend_tasks_m[N].md` - Backend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/frontend_tasks_m[N].md` - Frontend task breakdowns\n✓ `/src/field/ensemble_ui/output/test_tasks_m[N].md` - Test task breakdowns\n\n**Code Directories** (Specify for Spawned Agents):\nWhen spawning TDD Coordinator or Coordinators, tell them WHERE to write code:\n\n**Frontend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Backend Code Paths**:\n\n\n**Test Paths**:\n\n\n**When Spawning TDD Coordinator**, provide specific directories:\n\n\n### Process:\n\n**1. Read Requirements & Check Gaps**\nRead requirements file\n**BE DECISIVE**: Make reasonable technical decisions - ONLY ask if critical business decisions needed\nMissing: tech stack details → use modern defaults from requirements\nMissing: architecture patterns → use standard patterns (MVC, microservices, etc.)\nAmbiguous implementation → choose best practice approach\n**ONLY escalate when**: User must choose between major trade-offs (cost, security, compliance)\n\n**2. Create Milestones**\nBreak into logical, deliverable chunks\nEach milestone: objective, deliverables, acceptance criteria, dependencies\nWrite milestone plan document\n\n**3. Architecture - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool**: spawn_agent("leadership/system_architect", {requirements_file})\nReview System Architect\'s architecture output\nIf major decisions need user input → escalate to Executive Director\n\n**4. Task Breakdown (for FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Actually use spawn_agent tool**, don\'t just write task files\nFor milestone 1, spawn each Coordinator using spawn_agent with proper inputs:\nspawn_agent("coordinators/backend_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/developer_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/test_coordinator", {\n      "milestone": "description of milestone 1",\n      "architecture": "path/to/architecture.md",\n      "requirements": "path/to/requirements.md",\n      "output_file": "path/to/test_tasks.md"\n    })\nspawn_agent("coordinators/frontend_coordinator", {similar inputs})\nReview each Coordinator\'s output for task breakdown\nConsolidate task lists, identify dependencies\n\n**5. Implementation (FIRST milestone) - USE spawn_agent TOOL**\n**CRITICAL: Use spawn_agent tool to spawn TDD Coordinator with EXACT path**\n**EXACT PATH**: spawn_agent("leadership/tdd_coordinator", {\n    "problem_description": "description of what to build",\n    "output_directory": "where to put code",\n    "test_directory": "where to put tests (optional)",\n    "requirements_file": "path/to/requirements.md (optional)"\n  })\nTDD Coordinator orchestrates Section Techs/Leaders via TDD\nMonitor TDD Coordinator\'s progress\n**If spawn fails, STOP and return error with details**\n\n**6. Verify Milestone Complete**\nAll tasks done? Tests passing? Quality acceptable? Docs written?\nIf yes → next milestone (repeat 4-6); if no → fix\n\n**7. Project Complete**\nAll milestones done → verify deliverables, run tests, check docs\nCommit all changes to version control (see Git Workflow below)\nReport to Executive Director with status: `success`\n\n### Git Workflow:\n**IMPORTANT**: Commit changes after completing each milestone and at project completion.\n\n**When to commit**:\nAfter milestone planning documents are written\nAfter architecture and task breakdown phases\nAfter each milestone implementation completes\nBefore reporting final completion to Executive Director\n\n**How to commit**:\n\n\n**Commit message guidelines**:\nBe specific: "Complete milestone 1: user authentication backend"\nNot generic: ❌ "update", "changes", "milestone done"\nMention milestone number or phase\nMinimum 10 characters\n\n**Example**:\n\n\n### Workflow Per Milestone:\n\n\n### Your Authority:\nDetermine milestone breakdown\nApprove task plans from Coordinators\nDecide when milestones complete\nEscalate to Executive Director when needed\n\n### Escalate to Executive Director When:\nRequirements gaps\nArchitecture needs user approval\nMajor blockers or scope changes\nQuality issues unresolvable\n\n## Input Format\nYour input will be provided in the following format:\n```json\n{\n  "requirements_file": "string - path to requirements document",\n  "output_directory": "string - where to create artifacts",\n  "project_name": "string - project name"\n}\n```\n\n## Output Format\nYou must respond with JSON matching this exact format:\n```json\n{\n  "status": "success|in_progress|needs_clarification|failed",\n  "phase": "string - milestones|architecture|task_breakdown|implementation|complete",\n  "milestones": "array of milestones if created",\n  "deliverables": "array of paths to created files",\n  "clarification_needed": "string - questions for Executive Director (optional)",\n  "message": "string - status summary",\n  "self_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Your performance analysis (2-4 sentences)",\n  "performance_analysis": "string - REQUIRED: Analysis of System Architect, Coordinators, and TDD Coordinator performance (2-4 sentences)"\n}\n```\n\n## When to Request Clarification\nRequest clarification when:\n\n\n## Termination Conditions\nYou are done when:\n- All milestones completed, tests passing, documentation complete\n- Ready to report completion to Executive Director\n\nCRITICAL: Your response must be valid JSON matching the Output Format exactly.\n\n## Your Performance History\n- Success rate: 63.1%\n- Average iterations per task: 13.1\n- Common errors to avoid: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError, RateLimitError\n\n**Tips for this run:**\n- Focus on completing tasks successfully - your success rate needs improvement.\n- Try to be more efficient - you\'re using more iterations than typical.\n- Watch out for these common errors: CircuitBreakerOpenError, BadRequestError\n\n**Learnings from your recent runs:**\n- The project was executed with precision, maintaining the existing agent\'s structure while optimizing the model configuration. Each step was carefully coordinated to ensure minimal disruption and prese...\n- I effectively coordinated the model optimization project by breaking down requirements, engaging the System Architect, tracking project progress, and ensuring a successful implementation. The approach...\n', 'tools': [{'name': 'write_file', 'description': 'Write content to a file, creating parent directories if needed. Automatically backs up existing files.', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to write'}, 'content': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Content to write to the file'}}, 'required': ['file_path', 'content']}}, {'name': 'read_file', 'description': 'Read content from a file', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'file_path': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Path to the file to read'}}, 'required': ['file_path']}}, {'name': 'run_command', 'description': 'Execute a shell command and return the output', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'command': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'The shell command to execute'}, 'working_directory': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Optional working directory for command execution'}}, 'required': ['command']}}, {'name': 'git_commit', 'description': 'Commit changes to the git repository with a descriptive message', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'message': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Commit message describing the changes'}, 'files': {'type': 'array', 'items': {'type': 'string'}, 'description': 'Optional list of specific files to commit. If not provided, commits all modified files.'}}, 'required': ['message']}}, {'name': 'git_branch', 'description': 'Create, switch, list, or delete git branches for coordinated development', 'input_schema': {'type': 'object', 'properties': {'action': {'type': 'string', 'enum': ['create', 'switch', 'list', 'delete', 'current'], 'description': 'Action to perform: create new branch, switch to existing, list all, delete, or get current'}, 'branch_name': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Name of the branch (for create, switch, delete)'}, 'from_branch': {'type': 'string', 'description': 'Base branch to create from (for create, defaults to current branch)'}, 'force': {'type': 'boolean', 'description': 'Force the operation (for delete unmerged branches)', 'default': False}}, 'required': ['action']}}, {'name': 'git_merge', 'description': 'Merge branches or create pull requests for code review', 'input_sc